  "honest_limitations": [
    "MAGNITUDE has a documented SYSTEMATIC component: aliphatic ketones (MEK -20%, MIBK -20%, acetone -12%) and chloroalkanes (chloroform -18%) are UNDER-predicted, while polar aromatics (chlorobenzene +24%) are OVER-predicted -- the 4 core points outside +/-15%. Cause: gas-phase mu vs liquid effective moment and weak short-range dipolar ordering the g=1 Onsager cavity omits. Rank is unaffected (Spearman 0.995).",
    "ASSOC H-bonded liquids (water, C1-C4 mono-alcohols) are OUT-of-domain by construction: parallel dipole correlation (Kirkwood g>1) makes Onsager under-predict (water eps_pred ~29 vs 78.4). Reported, not hidden.",
    "BOUNDARY strongly-dipolar aprotics: MeCN shows antiparallel pairing (g<1) so Onsager OVER-predicts; DMF is at the high-mu edge and under-predicts ~10%. Reported apart from the core.",
    "Uses the gas-phase dipole moment mu; liquid-phase effective moment differs slightly (absorbed into the g=1 assumption).",
    "eps_s is the neat-SOLVENT static permittivity. Cured-film permittivity (the direct EIS/Brasher-Kingsbury input) is a Phase-1 extension requiring a network polarization model + rights-clean film data; NOT claimed here."
  ],
